WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.530
Two classes sit the same test.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:07.420
Their teacher announces: both classes
had a median mark of sixty-two.

3
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:12.020
Here are both classes' marks, plotted
as dots on the same mark scale,

4
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.950
one row for each class.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.780
The same middle mark.

6
00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:19.620
So does that mean the two
classes really did the same?

7
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.050
In this mission, you'll find
the median, the middle value,

8
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.920
and the quartiles, which split
ordered data into quarters.

9
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:32.480
You'll work out the interquartile range:
the upper quartile minus the lower quartile.

10
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.430
And you'll read quartiles from
a cumulative frequency graph.

11
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: decide whether the
two classes' results were the same.
